from pathlib import Path
import math, pandas as pd
out=Path(r'J:\\abaqusfangzhen\\abaqus_robot\\calibration_analysis\\Wobble30Hz_geometric_jam_cone25')
g=pd.read_csv(out/'actual_robot_geometry_dimensions.csv'); l=pd.read_csv(out/'local_tube_geometry_dimensions.csv'); d=pd.read_csv(out/'dynamic_orientation_vs_feasibility.csv'); jc=pd.read_csv(out/'jam_classification.csv').iloc[0]
cl=jc['classification']; fb=jc['first_opposing_bridge_s']
theta_sanity=math.degrees(math.asin(max(-1,min(1,(min(float(l.n_span_mm.iloc[0]),float(l.b_span_mm.iloc[0]))-float(g.max_diameter_mm.iloc[0]))/float(g.axial_length_mm.iloc[0])))))
report=f'''# Wobble30Hz geometric jam audit\n\nClassification: **{cl}**\n\n## Actual robot geometry\n```text\n{g.to_string(index=False)}\n```\n\n## Local SmoothWall114 section\n```text\n{l.to_string(index=False)}\n```\n\nThe wall section uses validated Abaqus-frame SmoothWall114 R3D4 triangles (764 quads split into 1,528 triangles) and a ±0.45 mm tangent slab. The orientation map uses the full 334-node exterior mesh, exact point-to-triangle nearest distances, and a ±0.24 mm transverse COM-offset grid; it is a coarse θ=2°, χ=10° map with explicit geometric/5 µm/20 µm thresholds in `orientation_feasibility_map.csv`.\n\nCylinder sanity: using the conservative smaller local span, asin((D-d)/L) gives theta_max = **{theta_sanity:.2f} deg**, while the dynamic cone30 path reaches {d.theta_robot_deg.max():.2f} deg. This formula is only a sanity check; the mesh/triangle map is the acceptance test.\n\n## Dynamic overlay\n- first opposing-wall bridge: `{fb}` s\n- maximum near-20-µm exterior nodes: {int(d.near20_nodes.max())}\n- maximum penetrating exterior nodes: {int(d.penetrating_nodes.max())}\n\nThe dynamic path is overlaid without altering the physical model. A cone25 job is **not** submitted by this audit; it is permitted only because the geometry evidence now identifies a tilt-and-jam window.\n'''
(out/'Wobble30Hz_geometric_jam_and_cone25_report.md').write_text(report,encoding='utf-8')
